  "note": "Triennial election of the councillors of Londonderry Corporation, due Wednesday 18 May 1955: there was no contest; the fifteen nominees were returned unopposed when nominations closed on Wednesday 4 May (Derry Journal, 6 May 1955, p. 5). The Journal calls the South Ward nominees Anti-Partitionists and prints no labels for the North and Waterside nominees. McFarland was the only newcomer; Milligan a former member. Returned unopposed."
